(a) **Housekeeping Services:**
(i) Daily sweeping, mopping, and cleaning of all common areas, including lobbies, staircases, corridors, lifts, and the clubhouse;
(ii) Cleaning and sanitization of washrooms in common areas and the clubhouse on a daily basis;
(iii) Garbage collection from each floor's garbage chute area and disposal as per municipal norms, twice daily (morning and evening);
(iv) Deep cleaning of common areas, including pressure washing of the podium and the main entrance, once every month;
(v) Cleaning of the Society's water tanks (both overhead and underground) once every quarter, with proper certification as required under local health regulations.

(b) **Gardening Services:**
(i) Maintenance of all landscaped areas, lawns, flower beds, and potted plants within the Society premises;
(ii) Weekly mowing of lawns, trimming of hedges, and pruning of trees and shrubs;
(iii) Daily watering of plants and lawns, with adjustments during monsoon and summer months;
(iv) Application of fertilizers, pesticides, and insecticides as required, using only approved chemicals and with prior intimation to the Society's Secretary;
(v) Replacement of dead plants and seasonal flowering plants, with the cost of plants being borne by the Society, provided that the Contractor gives at least 15 days' notice of the requirement.

(c) **Security Services:**
(i) Deployment of trained security guards at the main gate, the service gate, and the clubhouse, on a 24x7 basis, with three shifts of eight hours each;
(ii) The Contractor shall deploy a minimum of six (6) security guards at any given time, comprising two (2) guards at the main gate, one (1) guard at the service gate, and one (1) guard at the clubhouse, with the remaining two (2) guards on patrol duty within the premises;
(iii) Maintenance of a visitor register at both gates, recording entry and exit of all visitors, vendors, and service personnel;
(iv) Monitoring of CCTV cameras and reporting of any suspicious activity or security breach to the Society's Security Committee immediately, but in no case later than 15 minutes of noticing such activity;
(v) Verification of credentials of all new domestic staff employed by residents, including police verification where required, at no additional cost to the Society.

(d) **Minor Repairs:**
(i) Attending to minor civil, electrical, and plumbing repairs within the common areas and in individual flats, on a request basis through the Society's complaint management system;
(ii) The Contractor shall maintain a team of at least one (1) electrician, one (1) plumber, and one (1) carpenter available on site during working hours (9:00 AM to 6:00 PM) on all days except Sundays and public holidays;
(iii) For emergency repairs (such as major water leakage, electrical short-circuit, lift failure, or sewage blockage), the Contractor shall respond within 30 minutes of notification, including on Sundays and public holidays;
(iv) The cost of spare parts and materials required for repairs shall be borne by the Society, provided that the Contractor obtains prior approval from the Society's Secretary for any material costing more than Rs. 2,000 (Rupees Two Thousand only). For materials costing up to Rs. 2,000, the Contractor may procure the same and submit bills for reimbursement on a weekly basis.

**MAINTENANCE SERVICES CONTRACT**

*THIS CONTRACT* is made and entered into at Pune on this 1st day of April, 2024, by and between:

**THE PARYATAN CO-OPERATIVE HOUSING SOCIETY LIMITED**, a Co-operative Housing Society duly registered under the Maharashtra Co-operative Societies Act, 1960, having its registered office at Plot No. 14, S.No. 89/2, FC Road, Shivajinagar, Pune – 411005, hereinafter referred to as the "Society" (which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, be deemed to mean and include its successors-in-title and permitted assigns) of the FIRST PART;

**AND**

**M/s. GREENLEAF MAINTENANCE SERVICES**, a proprietorship firm having its office at Shop No. 3, Ground Floor, "Sai Plaza", Jangali Maharaj Road, Pune – 411005, represented by its Proprietor, Mr. Ramesh V. Kulkarni, hereinafter referred to as the "Contractor" (which expression shall, unless repugnant to the context or meaning thereof, be deemed to mean and include its heirs, successors, and assigns) of the SECOND PART.

The Society and the Contractor are hereinafter individually referred to as a "Party" and collectively as the "Parties".

**WHEREAS** the Society is desirous of engaging a competent and experienced contractor for the provision of housekeeping, sanitation, and general maintenance services for its premises, and the Contractor has represented that it possesses the requisite expertise, manpower, and resources to provide such services;

**AND WHEREAS** the Managing Committee of the Society, by its resolution passed at its meeting held on 15th March 2024, has authorised the execution of this Contract with the Contractor, and the Contractor has agreed to render the said services on the terms and conditions hereinafter appearing.

**NOW, THEREFORE, THIS CONTRACT WITNESSETH AND THE PARTIES HEREBY AGREE AS FOLLOWS:**

**ARTICLE 1: DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION**

1.1 In this Contract, unless the context otherwise requires:
(a) "Contract Amount" means the monthly contract amount payable to the Contractor as set out in Clause 4.1;
(b) "Commencement Date" means the 1st day of April, 2024;
(c) "Contract Period" means the period commencing from the Commencement Date and expiring on the 31st day of May, 2025, unless terminated earlier in accordance with the provisions of this Contract;
(d) "Services" means the services described in Schedule A hereto;
(e) "Society's Premises" means the building and common areas of the Society, including the compound, staircases, lobbies, lifts, parking areas, and such other areas as may be designated by the Society from time to time.

1.2 Words importing the singular shall include the plural and vice versa. Words importing the masculine gender shall include the feminine gender. Clause headings are for convenience only and shall not affect the interpretation of this Contract.

**ARTICLE 2: SCOPE OF SERVICES**

2.1 The Contractor shall provide the Services at the Society's Premises, in a professional and workmanlike manner, and in accordance with the standards and specifications set out in Schedule A.

2.2 The Contractor shall deploy the number of personnel and categories of staff as specified in the Staff Deployment Schedule set out in Schedule B.

2.3 The Contractor shall ensure that all personnel deployed by it:
(a) are adequately trained and competent to perform the duties assigned to them;
(b) are neatly and uniformly dressed, bearing a visible identity card issued by the Contractor;
(c) are of good character and conduct, and have been verified by the Contractor prior to deployment;
(d) abide by the rules, regulations, and bye-laws of the Society, and follow the instructions of the Society's authorised representative.
